* Sat Sep 26 2026 Jeremy Melanson <1080872+zish@users.noreply.github.com> - 1.0.0-1
- First package. The kiosk session: a greeter entry and the wrapper that is
  cage's child, so Waydroid's Android is the whole machine full-screen and an
  in-Android power-off lands back at the greeter (docs/25).
- The wrapper exists because `cage -- waydroid show-full-ui` cannot work: cage
  exits when its child exits and show-full-ui does not block once a session is
  tracked, this image's guest framework never announces its own shutdown, and
  cage starts no graphical-session.target for docs/24's backstop to hang off.
- A stale session is cleared rather than reused. The container binds the
  compositor's Wayland socket by inode and cage unlinks its socket on exit, so
  an inherited session holds a dead inode a new cage does not restore.
- The session entry ships in /usr/share/wayland-sessions and not the
  installer's /etc default, following waydroid-ext-backlight's 2026-09-24
  precedent -- and because SDDM's compiled-in SessionDir covers the /usr path
  while /etc is read on this host only via an unpackaged drop-in. Provisional:
  the host still carries a hand-placed /etc copy that a migration must delete.
- Enables nothing and defaults nothing: the entry is additive, and which session
  the machine logs into stays the administrator's decision.
- waydroid-graceful-exit is deliberately a separate modification (docs/24): its
  sway hook and user unit have nothing to do with a kiosk. The dependency is
  weak because the wrapper guards its absence and degrades to a hard kill.
